    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100-a1">

                <pb facs="0359" n="989" xml:id="pg989"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Appendix A.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName type="from">Castelar</persName> to
                        General <persName corresp="#p_DES1" type="to"
                    >Sickles</persName></hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State, private office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 8, 1873</date>.
                        (Received May 8.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Unofficial.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Friend</hi>: The inclosed is a copy of a
                    telegram from Havana which I wish I could have shown you in person so that we
                    could speak of matters of much interest to me and which will also interest you.
                    However, I will go to see you at my usual hour. I have again telegraphed for the
                    promised information about Santa Rosa.</p>
                <p>I remain. &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName>EMILIO CASTELAR</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
